          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "The prestige residential market in the Mornington Peninsula—spanning the clifftop enclaves of **Portsea and Sorrento**, the acreages of **Red Hill and Main Ridge**, and the coastal estates of **Flinders, Mount Eliza, and Mount Martha**—is dominated by a select group of luxury specialist agencies and premier auctioneers.\n\nBecause ultra-luxury properties ($10M+) in the Peninsula are frequently transacted via **Expressions of Interest (EOI)** or discrete off-market negotiations, top auctioneers in this region are prized both for their on-the-day podium performance and for their high-stakes private boardroom negotiation skills.\n\n---\n\n### **1. Leading Luxury Real Estate Agencies**\n\n#### **Peninsula Sotheby’s International Realty**\n* **Offices:** Sorrento, Flinders\n* **Market Position:** Widely regarded as a dominant force in the ultra-prestige segment. They represent a significant share of properties transacted above $5M to $30M+ across Portsea, Sorrento, and the hinterland. Their direct link to international luxury networks and Melbourne’s prime buyers makes them a first port of call for trophy estates.\n\n#### **Kay & Burton**\n* **Offices:** Portsea, Flinders\n* **Market Position:** Historically one of Melbourne’s and the Peninsula’s most venerable prestige brands. Kay & Burton operates a seamless pipeline between Melbourne’s wealthy inner-east (Toorak, South Yarra) and the Peninsula’s coastal retreats. They excel in clifftop compounds, landmark architectural builds, and secluded coastal acreages.\n\n#### **RT Edgar**\n* **Offices:** Portsea, Flinders\n* **Market Position:** RT Edgar has operated on the Peninsula since the 1930s and has brokered many of the region’s historic sales records. They retain deep generational connections with long-time landholders and high-net-worth holidaymakers.\n\n#### **Marshall White**\n* **Offices:** Sorrento, Flinders, Mount Eliza\n* **Market Position:** One of Melbourne’s largest prestige powerhouses, Marshall White has established a substantial presence on the Peninsula. They bring an extensive database of active buyers from Melbourne’s Bayside and inner suburbs, running sophisticated multi-channel campaigns.\n\n#### **WHITEFOX Real Estate (Peninsula)**\n* **Office:** Red Hill\n* **Market Position:** A modern, high-energy disruptor known for aggressive digital marketing, luxury styling, and strong auction room performance. They actively handle designer homes, coastal modern retreats, and lifestyle properties across Red Hill, Flinders, and Portsea.\n\n#### **McEwing & Partners**\n* **Offices:** Mornington, Mount Martha\n* **Market Position:** While agencies like Sotheby’s and RT Edgar dominate Portsea and Flinders, McEwing & Partners remains the benchmark boutique agency for the northern Peninsula (Mount Eliza, Mount Martha, and Mornington clifftops).\n\n---\n\n### **2. Top-Performing Prestige Agents & Auctioneers**\n\n* **Rob Curtain (Managing Director, Peninsula Sotheby’s International Realty)**\n  * **Specialisation:** Portsea, Sorrento, Flinders trophy estates.\n  * **Reputation:** Consistently one of Victoria’s top-transacting agents by dollar volume. Known as the key gatekeeper for the peninsula's premier $10M–$40M+ listings, with unmatched local knowledge and discreet off-market dealmaking.\n\n* **Warwick Anderson & David Gillham (Directors & Auctioneers, RT Edgar Portsea/Sorrento)**\n  * **Specialisation:** Clifftop properties, Portsea village, Sorrento back beach.\n  * **Reputation:** Both are veteran negotiators and licensed auctioneers with decades of combined experience. Gillham and Anderson are deeply trusted by generational Peninsula families and are renowned for managing high-profile campaigns.\n\n* **Liz Jensen (Director, Kay & Burton Portsea/Sorrento)**\n  * **Specialisation:** Portsea, Sorrento, Blairgowrie luxury residences.\n  * **Reputation:** Long acknowledged as one of the most successful female prestige agents in Australia. She has represented buyers and sellers across many of the Peninsula's most celebrated waterfront estates.\n\n* **Marty Fox (Founder/Auctioneer, WHITEFOX)**\n  * **Specialisation:** High-end architectural homes, modern coastal retreats.\n  * **Reputation:** Widely recognized as one of Victoria’s most dynamic auctioneers. He frequently flies or travels down to call competitive, theatrical on-site auctions that command strong emotional bidding.\n\n* **Stephen Baster & Andrew Hayne (Marshall White Sorrento & Flinders)**\n  * **Specialisation:** Southern Peninsula beachside homes, acreage, lifestyle properties.\n  * **Reputation:** Former Group 1 jockey Stephen Baster has emerged as a top-producing agent across the Mornington Peninsula. Combined with seasoned auctioneers like Andrew Hayne and group director John Bongiorno, Marshall White regularly posts top clearance rates in the $3M–$10M bracket.\n\n* **Dean Phillips & Quentin McEwing (McEwing & Partners)**\n  * **Specialisation:** Mount Martha (Esplanade), Mount Eliza (Golden Mile).\n  * **Reputation:** Dean Phillips is an accomplished auctioneer and agent specializing in luxury family retreats and architectural beachfront homes along the western coastline of the Peninsula.\n\n---\n\n### **Key Takeaway for Sellers & Buyers**\n* **For Clifftop / Historic Waterfront Trophy Homes ($10M+):** **Peninsula Sotheby’s** (Rob Curtain), **Kay & Burton** (Liz Jensen), and **RT Edgar** (Warwick Anderson / David Gillham) hold the strongest historical market share and international/interstate database access.\n* **For Competitive On-Site Auctions ($2M–$8M Designer & Holiday Homes):** **WHITEFOX**, **Marshall White**, and **RT Edgar** excel with auction energy, draw large crowds, and leverage Melbourne buyer crossover effectively.",
